  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Late rallies are becoming the spine of who this team is.",
    "what_this_means": "Eldridge had been quiet for stretches, but he found the middle of three balls in the third and fourth. Jung Hoo Lee kept adding runners. Then the game slipped away in the Cardinal half. Three runs in one inning turned a 1\u20130 lead into a 4\u20131 hole by the fifth. They trailed until the eighth. Whitcomb's double broke a 6\u20136 tie with one swing. That was the game. The bullpen never blinked after that: Abner threw two clean frames, Wilkinson struck out two in his two, Harris locked the door. This was not a comeback. This was a team that lost its lead, went silent for three innings, then took the game back because they knew how to finish it. The roster is thin and the record is bad, but winning one-run games at home against division rivals is not an accident three times in five days.",
    "what_to_watch": "Robbie Ray takes the mound for San Diego tonight at 7:15, and his 3.39 ERA has been built on keeping the lineup off balance early. Anthony Molina will be tasked with matching that precision.",
